{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772650970,"nonce":"AaXn8wvxoH8HNgA1JoY/nsVKpE0=","title":"mandible auth request: auto-detects wrong target branch for repos with develop as protected","message":"In repos where `develop` is the protected branch, `mandible auth request` always submits auth requests targeting `develop` even when the user explicitly wants to merge a feature branch into `main` (the repo default branch, not protected).\n\n**Incident (2026-03-03, feedbax repo):** Attempting to merge `feature/feedbax-claude-md-main` → `main` resulted in auto-detecting `develop` as target, merging wrong branch (325 files changed).\n\n**Root cause:** `auth-request.sh` reads the protected branch from `.dotfiles` config, which is always `develop` for feedbax. There is no way to easily specify \"I want this to go to `main`, not `develop`\" without bypassing the CLI.\n\n**Impact:** Any merge of non-feature-work content into the repos default branch (e.g., adding CLAUDE.md to `main`, documentation) will be incorrectly targeted at `develop`.\n\n**Status:** Fixed in dotfiles retro-fixes branch. This issue tracks the fix landing in the standalone repo.\n\nMigrated from dotfiles issue c6bd770.","files":null}]}